1
00:00:00,295 --> 00:00:06,395
In February 2020, ACTT-1 registered a
seven-point ordinal scale at day fifteen.

2
00:00:06,395 --> 00:00:08,736
The paper reports time to recovery.

3
00:00:08,736 --> 00:00:14,266
The registry says that outcome changed on
April sixteenth, in version fourteen of twenty-five.

4
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:18,773
Protocol Mirror found that from the live registry—
and it cannot decide what the change means.

5
00:00:19,764 --> 00:00:22,436
This is not a slideshow of invented data.

6
00:00:22,436 --> 00:00:26,861
The page opens on real ClinicalTrials.gov
and PubMed records.

7
00:00:26,861 --> 00:00:35,035
Seven typed WebMCP tools let the agent read the trial,
its publication, and the registration history as untrusted evidence.

8
00:00:36,028 --> 00:00:42,849
The agent retrieves the exact original registry span
and the paper's results, including stable source locators.

9
00:00:42,849 --> 00:00:49,613
It can inspect, cite, and stage a schema-bound proposal—
but it cannot accept or reject its own conclusion.

10
00:00:50,657 --> 00:00:53,691
Here, it proposes an uncertain relationship.

11
00:00:53,691 --> 00:01:02,843
The evidence stays visible beside the rationale, so the reviewer can inspect
the seven-point scale, the recovery result, and the dates instead of trusting a black-box summary.

12
00:01:03,909 --> 00:01:06,011
The reviewer can reject with a reason.

13
00:01:06,011 --> 00:01:11,508
That feedback returns through the audit state,
allowing the agent to revise and propose again.

14
00:01:11,508 --> 00:01:14,600
The two-way loop improves the work
without transferring authority.

15
00:01:15,624 --> 00:01:19,441
When the human accepts,
the page changes from seven tools to eight.

16
00:01:19,441 --> 00:01:22,453
Only then can the agent export a reviewed receipt.

17
00:01:22,453 --> 00:01:30,446
The receipt identifies live sources, preserves the history-zero locator,
and records the staged, rejected, revised, and accepted events.

18
00:01:31,450 --> 00:01:34,888
We also tested twenty-four real
trial-publication pairs.

19
00:01:34,888 --> 00:01:39,898
All forty-eight live source reads returned
the requested record with nonempty evidence.

20
00:01:39,898 --> 00:01:46,626
Two small local models then failed in opposite directions—
one overcalled changes while the other often missed them.

21
00:01:46,626 --> 00:01:50,295
These are run-specific grounding results,
not clinical validation.

22
00:01:51,335 --> 00:01:57,002
Protocol Mirror gives the agent the investigation,
citation, revision, and packaging work.

23
00:01:57,002 --> 00:02:00,334
A person remains accountable
for the consequential judgment.

24
00:02:00,334 --> 00:02:06,460
It is a research-transparency aid—not medical advice,
a misconduct detector, or a clinical decision system.
